				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/faustov" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1282427); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1282427&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605841712" alt="FaustoV" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1282427)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/faustov" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1282427); return false;" >FaustoV</a></span> <span class="odate time_1437234931 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Jul 2015 15:55</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2340634">
									

<p>And my problem with is that this article is just competent. That's all. You took an old article, fixed what needed to be fixed, included an emotional hook, and that's all. You see, maybe I'm biased, but since the Author is Djoric, I expect far more than that. From my point of view, you could have added more not just to improve the article, like exploring further into the origins of the skip. For instance, archaeologists are able to reconstruct History throughout pieces of ancient artifacts.</p>
<p>Imagine you're a SCP researcher and you're reading this. At the end, you will assume what the skip is, because you're not stupid, and wonder why the person who wrote this didn't give a formal but personal interpretation of what could've happened. It's more than obvious what the thing is. And the way you give all the puzzle pieces and refuse to solve it make the article feels incomplete instead of &quot;cold&quot;.</p>
<p>Overall, it feels like a lazy rewrite, so I'm downvoting it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
